--- THE ALIGNMENT STATISTICS (corrected: folded-angle tests) ---
  n = 59; mean delta = 49.0 deg (uniform: 45), bootstrap 95% CI [42.1, 55.9]
  mean |cos delta| = 0.584 (uniform: 0.637; AQUAL-aligned: ->1)
  chi2(8) = 7.36, p = 0.4988;  KS vs U(0,90): D = 0.135, p = 0.2108
  fraction delta < 15 deg (field-aligned): 0.119 (uniform: 0.167);  fraction delta > 75 deg (perpendicular): 0.169 (uniform: 0.167)
  median eps_Phi(mu2, eta_can) = 0.150  (AQUAL's predicted alignment amplitude)
  [PASS] K1: the dSph major axes do NOT concentrate along the GC bearing (field-aligned fraction = 0.119 vs 0.167 uniform; chi2 p = 0.4988) -- the field-aligned AQUAL elongation is ABSENT on this channel
  [PASS] K2: the delta-distribution is consistent with uniform (chi2 p = 0.4988, KS p = 0.2108, mean 49.0 deg within the bootstrap CI of 45) -- the direction-blind rule SURVIVES on the dSph channel
  [PASS] K3 (recorded): AQUAL's predicted eps_Phi(mu2) at the MW satellites is 0.150 (5-15%); the measured shapes show no such field-aligned component at the 3-sigma level -- the framework's magnitude-yes/direction-no fingerprint HOLDS on this channel (tidal alignment remains the allowed alternative, not tested here)

